  The article says the rice was seized and the two men were arrested in Valasaiyur area of Salem, but the draft's reel_script and captions place it as 'Veeranam' — the article only says Valasaiyur is 'adjacent to Veeranam' (வீராணத்தை அடுத்த), so the location is shifted and Veeranam is presented as the place of the seizure.
  The reel_script says the raid happened where a suspicious mini van was 'நின்ற' (standing) — the article does not say the van was standing; this is an added detail.
  The reel_script states the van contained the 1100 kg rice and that the seizure happened 'வேனில் இருந்த' — consistent, but the caption's 'நடவடிக்கை' line and slides attribute the arrests to the same police action without noting the video that triggered the operation in a clear sentence; the reel_script's sentence 'வீடியோ பரவியதும் நினைவுகூரத்தக்கது' is ungrammatical/unclear in Tamil and does not clearly state that a video showing rice being loaded into a van went viral.
  The reel_script's sentence 'கிடங்கில் பதுக்கி வைக்கப்பட்ட அரிசி மூட்டைகளை வேனில் ஏற்றும் வீடியோ பரவியதும்' mixes the viral video and the complaint into one unclear statement, merging two facts.
  The caption and slides state the raid was on 'திங்கள்கிழமை' and the caption adds a date '16 நவம்பர் 2026'; the article gives only the weekday (திங்கள்கிழமை), so the specific date is an invented detail.
